# No `dist/` here. This package's bundle IS the shipped artifact: it is committed
# and read back at export time (`server/src/modules/ci/files.ts` → BUNDLE_PATH).
# A `dist/` rule in THIS file would win over the root .gitignore's
# `!agent-runner/dist/**` re-include — git cannot re-include a path that a
# nested .gitignore excludes — leaving the bundle permanently untracked.
node_modules
*.log
